the new American Embassy to Israel is  open tonight in Jerusalem and that is  sparking a wide range of emotions from  jubilation among Israel and its  supporters in the Trump administration  to deadly rage from Palestinians and  their supporters throughout the world  while the president's daughter Ivanka  fronted a huge delegation from her  father's office  Palestinians clashed with Israeli troops  on the Gaza border resulting in dozens  of deaths and thousands of injuries that  is where we start tonight with  correspondent Benjamin Hall a campaign  promise fulfills today and with great  fanfare as the new US Embassy opened in  Jerusalem twenty-five years after  America first pledged to do so what a  glorious day remember this moment  President Trump by recognizing history  you have made history there was a  sizable US delegation among them Ivanka  Trump and Jared Kushner Stephen minuchin  and various members of Congress although  the president was not in attendance he  addressed the ceremony by video link  congratulations it's been a long time  coming the United States will always be  a great friend of Israel and a partner  in the cause of freedom and peace not  everyone was celebrating 53 miles south  the move inflamed the protests in Gaza  some 40,000 Palestinians staged  demonstrations along the border with  Israel leading to deadly clashes over 50  people were killed more than 2,300  wounded this has been the biggest  protest carried out by the Palestinians  since the protests began six weeks ago  it's also seen the biggest response from  the Israelis making this the deadliest  day since the war in 2014  Israeli military officials say they  foiled several coordinated attempts by  Palestinians to breach the fence pushing  them back with live fire they also  carried out airstrikes on Hamas camps  having warned the Palestinians in  advance we have to be very clear and  sharp and if needed forceful to defend  our border because Israeli civilians  lives are at stake  Estonian leaders say the move has ended  their trust in America forcing them to  walk away from peace talks  we considered America's embassy means  the end American control we will not go  back again to an American more protests  are planned tomorrow to commemorate what  Palestinians call the catastrophe of the  creation of the Jewish state but in  Israel today little can dampen the joy  at America's clear sign of commitment to  them a sentiment shared across political  divides has even Senate Minority Leader  Chuck Schumer praised the president for  moving the embassy saying he applauded  President Trump for doing so and only  two countries Guatemala and Paraguay  have said they'll follow suit and move  their embassy to Jerusalem and in news  just breaking in the last few hours  Turkey has just announced it is going to  put out its ambassador from the US both  in response to the move of the embassy  but also to the deaths of those  Palestinians and that is a big  diplomatic shift Brett  Benjamin Hall in Jerusalem Benjamin  thank you
 

